        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>\u201cHey ChatGPT, where\u2019s a good place to get coffee around here?\u201d Thanks to its new ability to peek at your location data, ChatGPT can now give you much better answers about what\u2019s nearby. That said, there\u2019s no reason to let ChatGPT know where you are at all times.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>First, the background. OpenAI recently rolled out the ability for ChatGPT to use your precise location when answering queries in a web browser and on iOS (Android is coming soon). ChatGPT\u2019s access to your location data is strictly an opt-in affair, meaning you must actively turn it on by going to the Settings menu, tapping on Data Controls, and then tapping Location Services.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>With the setting turned on, ChatGPT can pinpoint your location just as well as Google Maps and Apple Maps can, perfect for when you\u2019re out and about and want ChatGPT\u2019s help finding the closest cup of joe.</p",
